  "title": "A07: the writer for opaque strings and numbers",
  "op": "publish",
  "checks": [],
  "synthetic": true,
  "notes": [
    "RULINGS Q53a (A07), SPEC 9 item 7. The payload's string holds U+007F, the five characters with short escapes, U+0001,",
    "a slash, U+2028 and a lone surrogate (\\ud800, legal JSON escape grammar). It is written \"\\u007f\\b\\f\\n\\r\\t\\u0001/\\u2028\\ud800\":",
    "every character outside U+0020 to U+007E is escaped, \\b \\t \\n \\f \\r use their short forms, others use \\u with",
    "lowercase hex, and the slash is not escaped. The numbers -0, 1E3, 1.50 and a 30-digit integer are written 0, 1E3, 1.50",
    "and the same 30 digits: integer tokens as integers, other number tokens as their source text. The keys \"9\" and \"10\"",
    "sort by code point, \"10\" first (a JavaScript object would put the array-index keys in numeric order)."
  ],
